{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p>In&nbsp;<math alttext=\"triangle upper J upper K upper L\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>J</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></math>, the measures of both <math alttext=\"angle upper J\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>J</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper K\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>K</mi></math> are equal and the&nbsp;measure of <math alttext=\"angle upper L\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>L</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"118 degree\"><mrow><mn>118</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. What is the measure of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper J\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>J</mi></math>?</p>", "keys": ["f5db5455-0719-4561-84a2-16d735fbd5d3"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "f5db5455-0719-4561-84a2-16d735fbd5d3", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"31 degree\"><mn>31</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}, {"id": "3fc3f8d5-573c-4cf7-ac36-e431612068f7", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"59 degree\"><mn>59</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}, {"id": "4d727ef7-eec9-47ef-b2cd-f66819e1f392", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"62 degree\"><mn>62</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}, {"id": "f7fc7cc3-8228-44ce-b71e-7b4d4e896404", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"90 degree\"><mn>90</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. The sum of the measures of the three angles in a triangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It's given that in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"triangle upper J upper K upper L\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>J</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></math>, the measure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper L\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>L</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"118 degree\"><mn>118</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> represent the measure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper J\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>J</mi></math>.&nbsp;It's also given that the measures of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper J\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>J</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper K\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>K</mi></math> are equal, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> also represents the measure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper K\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>K</mi></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus x plus 118 equals 180\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>118</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 x plus 118 equals 180\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>118</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"118\"><mn>118</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 x equals 62\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>62</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 31\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></math>. Therefore, the measure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper J\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>J</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"31 degree\"><mn>31</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper J\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>J</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper K\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>K</mi></math>, not the measure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper J\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>J</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "60ddced0-ee94-414c-9143-3704d3c18d2e", "correct_answer": ["A"]}